{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
This land is [G]your land, and this land is [D]my land
From [A]California, to the New York [D]Island
From the Redwood [G]Forest, to the Gulf stream [D]waters,
[A]this land was made for you and [D]me
As I was [G]walking a ribbon of [D]highway
I saw [A]above me an endless [D]skyway[D7]
I saw [G]below me a golden [D]valley
[A]This land was [A7]made for you and [D]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I've roamed and rambled and I've followed my footsteps
To the sparkling sands of her diamond deserts
And all around me a voice was sounding
This land was made for you and me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
The sun comes shining as I was strolling
The wheat fields waving and the dust clouds rolling
The fog was lifting a voice come chanting
This land was made for you and me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
As I was walking, I saw a sign there
And that sign said, no trespassing
But on the other side, it didn't say nothin!
Now that side was made for you and me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
In the squares of the city - In the shadow of the steeple
Near the relief office - I see my people
And some are grumblin' and some are wonderin'
If this land's still made for you and me.
{end_of_chorus}
